language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Four friends each have one surname and one allergy. Print, for each allergy and each surname, the friend index (Debra=0, Janet=1, Hugh=2, Rick=3).
find eggs, mold, nuts, ragweed : int(0..3)
find baxter, lemon, malone, fleet : int(0..3)

branching on [eggs, mold, nuts, ragweed, baxter, lemon, malone, fleet]

such that
$ each friend has exactly one allergy, so the four allergies belong to four different friends
allDiff([eggs, mold, nuts, ragweed]),
$ each friend has exactly one surname, so the four surnames belong to four different friends
allDiff([baxter, lemon, malone, fleet]),
$ Rick is not allergic to mold
mold != 3,
$ Baxter is allergic to eggs: the friend with surname Baxter is the friend allergic to eggs
baxter = eggs,
$ Hugh is neither surnamed Lemon nor Fleet
lemon != 2,
fleet != 2,
$ Debra is allergic to ragweed
ragweed = 0,
$ Janet, who is not Lemon, is neither allergic to eggs nor to mold
lemon != 1,
eggs != 1,
mold != 1
